# netsurf: <progress> and <meter> render as bars; 203's accessors no longer leak (patch 218)
# Generated 2026-10-07
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser d531c3a (patch stack through 217)
#
# <progress> and <meter> had no UA styling and no rendering: they took no
# space (0 x one line) and drew their fallback text, if any, as plain
# inline content. Upload progress, reading-progress bars, quotas and
# ratings showed nothing.
#
#  - default.css: inline-block, border-box, 1em high, -0.2em
#    vertical-align, a #e6e6e6 track, overflow hidden; progress 10em wide
#    and meter 5em (Chromium: 160 x 16 and 80 x 16 at 16px).
#  - box_construct.c flags their boxes VB_PROGRESS (box.h), and redraw.c
#    paints the fill instead of the children (the fallback content is
#    not drawn): progress value / max (no value attribute -- the
#    indeterminate state -- a third of the track), meter
#    (value - min) / (max - min); accent-color when set, else blue
#    #0075ff / green #107c10. Attributes are read at paint time, so a
#    changed value repaints with the box.
#  - vita_polyfill.js: progress.value / .max set and read the attributes
#    and .position answers value / max (-1 when indeterminate). The
#    bridge's own HTMLMeterElement accessors are left alone: overriding
#    them did not take effect in the simulator (cause not found).
#
# Found while testing: tags the bridge has no constructor for share one
# generic element prototype, so patch 203's details/dialog accessors
# (open, show, showModal, close, returnValue) were on every such element.
# They now answer only for their own tag and behave as plain expando
# properties (undefined until set) elsewhere; the same holds for the
# progress accessors here.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/HTML-progress-meter.html (PROGRESS218, 5 checks,
# Chromium 5/5; without the patch the bars measured 0 wide): default
# sizes, a CSS width honoured and fallback text not growing the bar,
# value/max/position reflection, an indeterminate bar made determinate,
# and none of these properties appearing on a <div> or <section>.
# HIDDEN203 stays 9/9.
